/*
    Builder Design pattern is a creational design pattern
    it is used to create complex objects step by step without directly using the constructors.
    definition : it is used in when an object contains many optional fields and multiple combinations of constructors.
    why Builder Design pattern ?
    1.> Solves TeleScoping constructor problem
    2.> Improves readability of code
    3.> provide step by step Construction
    4.> Immutable Objects
    5.> Easy to maintain

    Real time use cases

    Use case                              where used
    1.> StringBuilder class               java APi
    2.> Spring Boot Builder               RestTemplate
    3.> Hibernate Criteria API            Complex Queries
    4.> Lombok @Builder                   Entity Classes


    Difference between Factory and Builder

    Factory                               Builder
    1.> create object in one step        1.> Step-by-step construction
    2.> Used When object is simple       2.> Used when object is complex
    3.> Tight coupling                   3.> loose coupling
    4.> no optional fields               4.> Handles Optional Fields

    How to make Builder Singleton ?
    just use Enum with Builder

    EX: Public enum PhoneBuilder{
    INSTANCE;
    public Phone getPhone(){
    return new Phone("8gb","128GB","64MP");
    }
    }

    can we break builder singleton with Cloning?
    no because Enum singleton is is 100% cloning proof+ reflection proof + serialization proof
     */